WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:04.840
The first trailer for Sony's Morbius does
an excellent job setting up the core story

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:10.360
of the film, a doctor transforms into a vampire
after attempting to cure his rare blood disease.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.500
But it also features subtler moments that
offer significance.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.780
These are the small details you missed in
the Morbius trailer.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.520
The first 45 seconds or so of the Morbius
trailer establish that the doctor is suffering

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.240
greatly because of his illness.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.880
He's shown with wires taped to his head and
neck, struggling to walk with forearm crutches,

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:32.419
and hunched over a bed as a fellow doctor
meticulously counts the vertebrae of his spine

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:33.800
protruding from his skin.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.440
In a voiceover, he says: "I'm running out
of time."

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:41.100
It soon becomes clear that Dr. Morbius intends
to cure his blood disease using non-traditional

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.600
medicine and his own devices, which raises
a red flag to the woman working alongside

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.100
him.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.340
When Morbius says that what he's discovered
would be a cure, she asks:

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.180
"At what cost?"

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:55.140
This line is more than just the musings of
a concerned colleague, it's foreshadowing

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.280
of the highest degree.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:01.620
The woman who speaks it is Martine Bancroft,
Morbius' fianceé played by Adria Arjona.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:06.640
Throughout the Marvel comics, Martine actually
dies several times, is resurrected, and eventually

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.680
becomes a living vampire herself.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:13.260
It's unclear at this point in time, however,
whether the Morbius film will depict the death,

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.980
subsequent revival, and transformation of
Martine.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.820
While several members of the Morbius cast
were announced far before the release of this

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:24.159
first trailer, one actor's involvement in
the film came as a complete surprise, and

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.080
was only revealed through the new footage.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:31.540
At the very end of the Morbius trailer, Michael
Keaton appears as Vulture, a.k.a. Adrian Toomes,

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.280
the villain of Spider-Man: Homecoming.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.880
"Got tired of doing the whole good guy thing,
huh?"

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:37.240
"What's up, Doc?"

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.500
Those who stuck around for the Spider-Man:
Homecoming post-credits scenes might recognize

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.880
what the salvager-slash-arms-trafficker is
wearing in the Morbius trailer.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.840
As a hooded Morbius approaches his white van,
Vulture is shown donning the same prison jumpsuit

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:54.040
he was wearing in Homecoming's mid-credits
stinger, pardon the, uhh, Scorpion pun.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:58.060
Anyway, since his appearance in the Morbius
trailer is so brief, there's no way to tell

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:02.560
when exactly the meeting between Vulture and
Morbius takes place in the movie's timeline.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.620
Because of that, it's also not clear how significant
Keaton's role in the film will be.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:09.500
That doesn't mean Keaton's appearance is all
for show and shock, though.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:14.260
Vulture's brief, end-of-trailer reveal might
allude to the early foundations for a potential

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.270
Sinister Six team-up on the silver screen.

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:20.420
While the Spider-Man villain team has had
numerous iterations in the comics, several

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:25.490
of its key or recurring baddies, including
Venom, Mysterio, Doctor Octopus, and Green

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:30.800
Goblin, have already appeared in both Sony's
Spidey offerings and its shared MCU installments.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:35.480
While nothing has been confirmed, Keaton's
surprise cameo in Morbius is much larger than

00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:39.830
the return of a famous face, it could signal
a more connected and expanding web of the

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:41.080
Spidey universe.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:45.340
With Sony launching, and planning to launch,
so many Spider-Verse movies, it's hard to

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:49.140
keep up with who and what we can expect to
see out of the growing web of adaptations.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:54.640
One image captured within the Morbius trailer
helps further that confusion, or air of mystery,

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:55.820
depending on whom you ask.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:03:00.600
In the first-look footage, in a blink-and-you'll-miss-it
moment, Morbius walks past a mural of Spider-Man

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:03.100
with the word "murderer" spray-painted across
it.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:07.220
There are a couple things to pull apart from
the moment, the first being Spidey's outfit.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:11.340
It appears to be a blend of several Spider-Man
suits, but looks most similar to Sam Raimi's

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:12.160
version.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:16.500
If you can remember all the way back to the
2000s, Tobey Maguire embodied the web-slinger

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:19.700
when Raimi's Spider-Man trilogy was dominating
silver screens.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:23.810
If you were a hardcore fan of those films,
you may have also bought the PlayStation 4

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:28.280
exclusive Spider-Man game featuring an animated
version of Peter Parker wearing a Raimi-like

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:32.620
suit, which is seemingly the same suit shown
in the mural that appears in the Morbius trailer.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:36.020
The second noticeable thing is the actual
language covering the image.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:40.640
The "murderer" statement points to Tom Holland's
most recent turn as Peter Parker in Spider-Man:

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:41.500
Far From Home.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:46.120
During the final scenes of that film, Peter
is accused of killing Mysterio using footage

00:03:46.129 --> 00:03:50.989
the villain doctored and sent to J. Jonah
Jameson, who broadcasted it in a video posted

00:03:50.989 --> 00:03:52.840
to TheDailyBugle.net.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.080
"Spider-Man's name is Peter Parker!"

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.020
"What the f—."

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:02.280
There's no clarity about what this moment
in the Morbius trailer could mean just yet,

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:06.080
but here's to hoping a legit Spidey cameo
happens in the theatrical cut.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.020
Later on in the trailer, there's a shot of
Matt Smith's character walking cautiously

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:12.380
through a seemingly abandoned subway station.

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:16.070
In the film, Smith doesn't play some random
tie-wearing dude who likes to walk around

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:18.480
alone at night, he plays Loxias Crown.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:23.680
Smith's Loxias Crown is to be the central
antagonist of Morbius, however, Smith's character

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.940
has been described as, quote, "Morbius' best
friend."

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.360
So, what's going on here?

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:32.320
In the Marvel comics, Crown is best known
as Hunger, another vampire whose origin is

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:36.729
unknown and who has nothing to do directly
with the events that lead to Morbius transforming

00:04:36.729 --> 00:04:38.100
into a pseudo-vampire.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:43.240
But there's also the character of Emil Nikos,
Dr. Morbius' closest friend and lab associate

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:48.460
who dies as a result of Morbius' post-transformation
confusion and bloodlust, only to be made into

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:51.660
a vampire by another unrelated comic character
later.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:55.880
Since Smith's character has Crown as a last
name, it's been assumed from the get-go that

00:04:55.889 --> 00:05:00.570
he's partially inspired by the preexisting
Marvel antagonist, and the rest of his characterization

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.440
is filled in by the general concept of Emil
Nikos.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:07.780
Smith's character will reportedly be afflicted
by the same blood disease Morbius is, which

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:12.730
is the basis of their friendship, and perhaps
its ultimate destruction, once Morbius kinda-sorta

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.560
cures and curses himself.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:19.320
The Morbius trailer also gives us a good look
at Tyrese Gibson's character, whom we know

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:23.039
from one of the actor's Instagram posts to
be FBI Agent Simon Stroud.

00:05:23.039 --> 00:05:27.550
In the pages of Marvel comics, Stroud is an
Agent-of-S.H.I.E.L.D.-turned-mercenary who

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:32.000
seems to always find himself tangled up with
the weirder denizens of the Marvel universe,

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.100
including Morbius.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:36.980
Stroud is sporting some interesting tech in
his brief appearance in the Morbius trailer.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:41.139
He's seen wearing a sleeve that appears to
offer augmentation for his right arm, and

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.460
specifically his hand.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:46.460
Stroud was never depicted as having any kind
of enhancements in the comics, and this one

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:49.360
raises an interesting question: Who built
the thing?

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:53.360
Stroud often worked side-by-side with Morbius
in the comics, and this tech looks like the

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.760
kind of thing that the good doctor, with his
Nobel Prize-winning expertise in physiology

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:59.740
and medicine, might have constructed.

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:02.440
Obviously, Stroud won't be depicted as a S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:06.400
agent in this film, as the Sony Universe of
Marvel Characters and the Marvel Cinematic

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:09.420
Universe are still ostensibly separate, for
now.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:13.760
Still, Stroud's dapper attire and the fact
that he's seen backed by a number of cops

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:18.590
seem to indicate that he'll be in some kind
of position of authority, meaning that Morbius

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:23.240
may very well have a friend in high places
to help unstick him from tricky situations.

